there are more than 600 muscles in the  human body  but if you're training for a main role  on riverdale only a small fraction of  those  really matter the chest shoulders and  abdominal v-cut  which stars like kj apa sculpt to look  great on camera  every role has its physical demands  whether it's all about aesthetics  acrobatics size or strength  let's take a look at the highly  customized training programs of  seven actors preparing for intensely  physical roles  michael b jordan is pretty much always  in great shape  but the body he sculpts in training  depends on the character he's getting  ready to play  the actor was fresh off his role as  adonis in creed  when he started gearing up to play  killmonger in black panther  both are very physical roles but they're  also very different  one is a boxing hero the other a super  villain  plus killmonger was michael's first time  playing a bad guy  so he had to do everything he could to  get in the character's head  and body michael's longtime trainer  corey kaye  said all these factors helped shape his  client's regimen  for michael to play adonis corey said  the goal was to get  lean lean lean the program involved a  lot of running  and surprise boxing but while the actors  creed training was all about getting  cut his black panther training was all  about getting  big michael and corey wanted to build a  body that would surprise people  so using the foundation he built for  creed michael ditched his high cardio  routine for intense weight training  built around  curls squats and bench presses corey is  also michael's nutritionist  and for black panther he had his client  eating five to six meals a day on a  carb-heavy diet that included lots of  potatoes  eggs bacon and chicken this helped  michael fill out his upper body and  ultimately add 15 pounds of muscle to  his frame  but right after black panther he headed  back into the ring for creed 2  which meant he and corey had to bring  back adonis all over again  each avenger has their own set of skills  natasha romanovs are her martial arts  when scarlett johansson landed the role  in 2009 she enlisted celebrity trainer  eric johnson to turn her into the deadly  assassin we see in the avengers movies  the first part of scarlet's training was  all about mobility  many of black widow's signature moves  are spider-inspired  like this leg twist attack where she  wraps her leg around the neck of her  opponent  that's a pretty high kick eric says and  it requires a lot of hip mobility and  hip flexor strength  he had scarlett do 90 90 hip swivels so  she could perform the move explosively  the second stage of her training was  aimed at building power  eric had scarlett doing a 245 pound  deadlift  and single leg pistol squats in this  phase of the training  that power translates on screen and  black widow's kicks and punches  like here in this scene from captain  america civil war  a lot of people think punches only come  from the arms or the upper body  but eric says that if you want to  produce power it has to come from the  ground  all the way up to that fist the third  and final phase  was geared toward getting scarlet at  peak conditioning level  this phase refined some aesthetic  aspects of scarlet's performance  for one eric had scarlett practice her  recovery after an intense set  gaining control of her breathing and  getting her heart rate down as fast as  possible  so that she could better control her  face on camera  after all she couldn't afford to have a  pain face on when playing black widow  she needed to look as poised and  controlled as a superhero would  if black widow's strength lies in her  punches and kicks spider-man's lies in  his agility and acrobatics  luckily tom holland has a background as  a dancer and  gymnast tom said he had to audition  eight times to play spider-man  and his athleticism ultimately helped  land him the role  even with his solid foundation though  tom had to train hard in preparation for  his first  solo marvel film spider-man homecoming  after all his acrobatics had to look  super human which meant convincingly  climbing walls  doing wild flips and slinging webs  through the city  here tom's following his stunt double  holland diaz and doing a side somersault  off a mini trampoline  followed by a big kick out and a perfect  left foot landing  when he wasn't in the gymnasium tom kept  his training up with an air track mat  a giant inflatable and portable piece of  equipment that's kind of like a spring  floor bouncy castle and tumbling and  landing that all wrapped up into one  he used this to practice his twists  flips  and side somersaults tom was determined  to do most of his own stunts  but he had to do crossfit style circuit  workouts to make sure he could work day  in  and day out on set to sharpen his spidey  reflexes  tom went through extensive martial arts  and combat training  here he is again with his stunt double  working on his hand-eye coordination  and then there was the question of  aesthetics filling out the spidey suit  and looking good out of the suit too one  of tom's trainers george ashwell said  the shirtless scene in the script  motivated tom to add 14 pounds of muscle  to his frame  the actor did sets of chin-ups to build  up his chest tom shared this photo with  marvel trainer duffy gaver on their last  workout day  showing off his body in peak spidey  shape  riverdale has been known for its  shirtless scenes from the beginning  but season 3 brought a new challenge for  star kj appa whose character archie  goes from high school football jock to  prison boxer  given the number of bare-chested fight  scenes he'd have to appear in  kj decided to step up his fitness  routine under the guidance of  alex fine the riverdale cast's secret  weapon  after getting a start doing strength  conditioning for nfl stars like odell  beckham jr  reggie bush and marshawn lynch alex went  on to train kj  charles melton cole sprouse camila  mendes casey cott  bart denton and mark consuelos actors  are different from athletes he says  for guys like kj or charles who plays  reggie on the show  alex will pay special attention to the  top of the chest and shoulders  since those areas are the most  noticeable on camera  for season three alex incorporated high  intensity cardio into kj's weight  training to help him get a lean waist  he had kj doing two 90-minute workouts a  day often they tackle cardio in the  morning and then do weights in the  afternoon  beyond basic weightlifting alex says  clients like kj do a lot of bodyweight  exercises  including sit ups planks push-ups  pull-ups and chin holes  this regimen has the advantage of using  minimal gym equipment  basically a prison cell workout alex  says  creating a bigger chest and leaner waist  gets clients like kj  closer to one of the aesthetic goals for  riverdale stars  sculpting that v-cut also known as the  sex lines  that's the deep v-shaped cut where the  lower abs and obliques meet  this is one role where vanity muscles  maybe  are the most important thing  bob odenkirk was a comedy writer for 25  years before  starring as tv's favorite lawyer a  decidedly  non-action role but at age 58 he starred  in his first ever action movie  nobody bob got a head start on bringing  out the fighter within  he started training for nobody before  the film was even greenlit  it's standard for an actor to train for  four to six  weeks for a role bob trained for two  years  as a guy in his 50s bob wanted to avoid  getting sidelined by an injury  for that reason his trainer stunt actor  daniel bernhardt  said that intense weight training like  lifting a heavy bench press  was not on the table instead bob's  training was all about  movement daniel gave him a crash course  in screen fighting based on the concept  of hip rotation  according to daniel fighting is all  about how you turn your hips when you  throw a punch  when you take a reaction for bob  learning to activate his hips  helped blast his core and provide him  with the explosive punch power he needed  for the bus fight in nobody  director ilya nae schuler wanted bob to  fight like a wolverine in that scene  the goal was for him to pull off 99 of  his own stunts so they wouldn't have to  use  fast-paced editing to hide bob's  mistakes or stunt replacements  that allowed ilya to get longer takes  that made the fight feel more visceral  and realistic  in the end it was okay for bob's  fighting skills to be rough around the  edges  that's because the bus fight is the  first time we see hutch transform back  into his fighter self  so his character is actually supposed to  look a little rusty  in the making and that's only the fight  bob odenkirk went from average to action  hero but what about becoming a  superhero that's what brie larson had to  do when she signed on to play one of the  most  powerful avengers for her standalone  movie captain marvel  free's character had to look believable  engaging her enemies in hand-to-hand  combat atop a moving train  the only problem brees started her  career in  indie roles and said she was never  particularly active before taking on the  role of carol danvers  at the beginning of training she  couldn't even do a proper push-up or  pull-up for her initial fitness  inspiration she looked to emily blunt  who got jacked for edge of tomorrow so  that she could safely wear a  70-pound exoskeleton bree sought out  emily's trainer jason walsh and with him  planned out a nine-month training  schedule  much of which would take place as brie  was shooting avengers end game  brie's body kept getting more taut as  training went on  forcing the costume team for captain  marvel to adjust her suit  more than once the staples of her  program included hip thrusts  split squats and the dreaded push-ups  and pull-ups  jason rarely has his clients use  machines but he and bree did get  creative with other equipment  like these weighted chains which they  wrapped around bree's torso to make her  push-up sets even more challenging  or jason's own car he said brie got it  in her head early on that she'd get  strong enough to push  jason's jeep with her bare hands and by  the end of training  she did for a full 60 seconds  so basically real life superhero stunts  the physicality brie achieved through  her transformation helped her  performance  but so did the mentality one of jason's  goals was to get brie as close as  humanly possible to the psychology of a  superhero  who was pretty much invincible in the  end he said  having that physical strength helped her  become the character  it wasn't painless jason said there were  points where he made brie cry  in the gym  when jennifer lopez and constance wu  played strippers and hustlers  they couldn't fall back on body doubles  for the pole dancing scenes  the film didn't use any which meant both  actors had to get  pole ready it was okay for constance wu  to look a little less experienced on the  pole  after all her character destiny is  supposed to be a newbie  j-lo on the other hand plays ramona a  veteran stripper at the club who takes  destiny under her wing  to fit this dynamic there had to be a  clear contrast between destiny's  beginner skills  and ramona's mastery of the poll  in other words j-lo had to nail it  she had danced before of course on tour  and in movies like shall we dance  but pole dancing is a whole different  ball game  it requires certain muscle groups to be  super strong  and no small amount of acrobatics that's  where pole choreographer johanna sepaki  came in  a former aerial acrobat in cirque du  soleil johanna designed  all the pole dancing scenes and hustlers  including ramona's  main routine which clocked in at 4  minutes long  jlo would have to do multiple takes of  that dance at different angles  getting it right every time to meet the  challenge the actor moved a portable  pole into each of her houses in new york  city  la and miami so that she could practice  all the time  johanna started her training with  climbing and basic spins  laying down the main principles of pole  dancing after that it took a while for  j.lo to develop a fast  smooth rotation on the pole spinning can  be disorienting at first  even if you're an experienced dancer  like j-lo as johanna explained  when you're a dancer you spin on top of  yourself as a pole dancer you're like a  carousel  going around a fixed point the last  thing to master was the inverted  splits this was supposed to be the one  big wow moment in ramona's routine  where she flips upside down on the pole  and supports her whole body with just  her arms and shoulders  inverting and then keeping that position  on the pole takes a lot of core strength  a lot of upper body strength and an  excellent grip  at first johanna would spot jlo as she  practiced pulling herself  up after two months of training though  jlo was comfortably doing  upside down splits on her own the actor  said that learning the pole dance was  one of the hardest things i've ever had  to do for a role  you
 

